{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שונאך", :translit "son'akha", :gloss "your enemy"} {:he "חמור שונאך", :translit "khamor son'akha", :gloss "the donkey of your enemy"} {:he "אם רעב שונאך האכילהו לחם", :translit "im ra'ev son'akha ha'akhilhu lekhem", :gloss "if your enemy is hungry, feed him bread"} {:he "וחדלת מעזוב לו", :translit "vekholata me'azov lo", :gloss "and you refrained from leaving it to him"} {:he "עזוב תעזוב עמו", :translit "azov ta'azov imo", :gloss "you shall surely leave with him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["חמור שונאך" "אם רעב שונאך"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase אם רעב שונאך האכילהו לחם derives from Proverbs 25:21. The Ba'al HaTurim cites a derash distinguishing between an enemy who is an idolater from the seven nations and one who is an Israelite. For the idolater, the verse's language וחדלת מעזוב לו (Exodus 23:5) implies you may refrain from helping; for the Israelite enemy, the doubled language עזוב תעזוב עמו (Deuteronomy 22:4) obligates you to help.", :sources ["Proverbs 25:21" "Exodus 23:5" "Deuteronomy 22:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "רובץ", :translit "rovets", :gloss "lying down"} {:he "לפתח חטאת רובץ", :translit "liftei khatat rovets", :gloss "at the door sin crouches"} {:he "רובץ בין המשפתים", :translit "rovets bein ha-mishpe'tim", :gloss "crouching between the sheepfolds"} {:he "יצה\"ר", :translit "yitzro hara", :gloss "the evil inclination"} {:he "משכהו לבית המדרש", :translit "meshakhehu le-veit ha-midrash", :gloss "drag him to the study hall"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["רובץ" "לפתח חטאת רובץ" "רובץ בין המשפתים"]}], :frame {:text "Genesis 4:7 describes sin crouching at the door: לפתח חטאת רובץ. The Talmud (Sukkah 52b) identifies the evil inclination by the phrase 'if this wretch encounters you, drag him to the study hall,' meaning Torah study is the remedy for overwhelming sin. Genesis 49:14 describes Issachar as a donkey crouching between the sheepfolds (רובץ בין המשפתים), here read as one who engages in Torah. The Ba'al HaTurim links the רובץ of the overloaded donkey to the remedy of Torah study.", :sources ["Genesis 4:7" "Genesis 49:14" "Sukkah 52b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "את תבואתה", :translit "et tevu'atah", :gloss "its produce"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The particle את, read as an inclusive addition, extends the prohibition to produce of the sixth year that carries into the seventh."}], :frame {:text "The Sages hold that the seventh year sanctifies whatever produce grows during it, even produce that began forming before the sabbatical year started. The Talmud (Rosh Hashanah 12b–13a) addresses produce of the sixth year whose growth extended into the seventh. The Ba'al HaTurim uses the extra את to extend תבואתה to include such produce.", :sources ["Rosh Hashanah 12b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["חמור שונאך" "אם רעב שונאך"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "חמור שונאך", :refs ["Exodus 23:5"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אם רעב שונאך", :refs ["Proverbs 25:21"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["רובץ" "לפתח חטאת רובץ" "רובץ בין המשפתים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "רובץ", :refs ["Genesis 4:7" "Genesis 49:9" "Genesis 49:14" "Exodus 23:5" "Isaiah 11:6" "Isaiah 11:7" "Isaiah 13:20" "Isaiah 13:21"], :n 14, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "לפתח חטאת רובץ", :refs ["Genesis 4:7"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "רובץ בין המשפתים", :refs ["Genesis 49:14"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "The particle את, read as an inclusive addition, extends the prohibition to produce of the sixth year that carries into the seventh.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:51.086260852Z", :model "glm-5.2"}